      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Hadoop 3.3.6 S3A does not publish buffered writes through hflush/hsync; publication occurs at close. Its downgrade-syncable-exceptions setting controls warning versus UnsupportedOperationException, not whether flushing persists data. This scopes any durability inference from the helper’s hflush. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://hadoop.apache.org/docs/r3.3.6/hadoop-aws/tools/hadoop-aws/troubleshooting_s3a.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:54e4f5c8cbca650d773b5ec9deec66fa15580920c1c999e83fff3f5ad5da5556",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:af592dba99677736fbb189dda80cc052051a0acf967eceee552a0631409ee476"
          ]
        }
      ]
