    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "In r10.5.0, initialOffset checks the supplied path. If it exists, it reads all bytes, decodes UTF-8 and calls MongoOffset.fromJson; otherwise it writes the configured initial offset. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo-spark/r10.5.0/src/main/java/com/mongodb/spark/sql/connector/read/MongoOffsetStore.java",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:8b4044a19872804eccfe55e7b24110e57aa34b0958aadbd05cae5a56f25c0914",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:8de224ab36f55507ecbd343a00966c297b3f8ccdeb5ceffcabb9bf070a36b469"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In r10.5.0, updateOffset calls fs.create(path, true), writes UTF-8 offset.json(), calls hflush(), and closes through try-with-resources. No temporary-path rename appears. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo-spark/r10.5.0/src/main/java/com/mongodb/spark/sql/connector/read/MongoOffsetStore.java",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:063309858fe302b0ec39414ee0aa1b43a09316e8c2fe888bff12938b372d8a15",
